1
00:00:01,330 --> 00:00:05,741
Chapter 32 I continued the labours of the village

2
00:00:05,743 --> 00:00:09,711
school as actively and faithfully as I could.

3
00:00:10,050 --> 00:00:12,410
It was truly hard work at first.

4
00:00:13,330 --> 00:00:16,514
Some time elapsed before, with all my efforts,

5
00:00:16,514 --> 00:00:19,510
I could comprehend my scholars and their nature.

6
00:00:20,089 --> 00:00:26,150
Holy untaught, with faculties quite torpedoed, they seemed to me hopelessly dull.

7
00:00:26,290 --> 00:00:29,550
And, at first sight, all dull alike.

8
00:00:30,349 --> 00:00:31,930
But I soon found I was mistaken.

9
00:00:33,089 --> 00:00:37,050
There was a difference amongst them, as amongst the educated.

10
00:00:37,769 --> 00:00:43,129
And when I got to know them, and they me, this difference rapidly developed itself.

11
00:00:44,230 --> 00:00:49,510
Their amazement at me, my language, my rules and ways, once subsided.

12
00:00:50,290 --> 00:00:52,671
I found some of these heavy-looking gaping

13
00:00:52,673 --> 00:00:56,391
rustics wake up into sharp, witted girls enough.

14
00:00:56,849 --> 00:00:59,690
Many showed themselves obliging and amiable too.

15
00:01:00,610 --> 00:01:05,910
And I discovered amongst them, not a few examples of natural politeness,

16
00:01:06,510 --> 00:01:10,360
and innate self-respect, as well as of excellent

17
00:01:10,360 --> 00:01:14,529
capacity that one both my good will and my admiration.

18
00:01:15,370 --> 00:01:20,949
These soon took a pleasure in doing their work well, in keeping their persons neat,

19
00:01:21,809 --> 00:01:26,550
in learning their tasks regularly, in acquiring quiet and orderly manners.

20
00:01:27,309 --> 00:01:32,269
The rapidity of their progress, in some instances, was even surprising.

21
00:01:33,129 --> 00:01:35,769
And an honest and happy pride I took in it.

22
00:01:36,790 --> 00:01:41,690
Besides, I began personally to like some of the best girls, and they liked me.

23
00:01:42,809 --> 00:01:48,569
I had amongst my scholars several farmers' daughters, young women grown almost.

24
00:01:49,389 --> 00:01:52,069
These could already read right and so.

25
00:01:53,510 --> 00:01:56,489
And to them I taught the elements of grammar,

26
00:01:56,491 --> 00:01:59,690
geography, history, and the finer kinds of needlework.

27
00:02:00,510 --> 00:02:06,870
I found estimable characters amongst them, characters desirous of information and

28
00:02:06,870 --> 00:02:09,940
disposed for improvement, with whom I passed

29
00:02:09,940 --> 00:02:13,069
many a pleasant evening hour in their own homes.

30
00:02:13,650 --> 00:02:20,190
Their parents then, the farmer and his wife, loaded me with attentions.

31
00:02:20,650 --> 00:02:27,290
There was an enjoyment in accepting their simple kindness, and in repaying it by a

32
00:02:27,290 --> 00:02:33,069
consideration, a scrupulous regard to their feelings, to which they were not,

33
00:02:33,269 --> 00:02:38,250
perhaps, at all times accustomed, and which both charmed and benefited them.

34
00:02:38,849 --> 00:02:43,949
Because, while it elevated them in their own eyes, it made

35
00:02:43,949 --> 00:02:47,730
them emulous to merit the deferential treatment they received.

36
00:02:48,529 --> 00:02:51,349
I felt I became a favorite in the neighborhood.

37
00:02:52,089 --> 00:02:56,211
Whenever I went out, I heard on all sides cordial

38
00:02:56,211 --> 00:03:00,190
salutations, and was welcomed with friendly smiles.

39
00:03:01,629 --> 00:03:06,290
To live amidst general regard, though it be but the regard of working

40
00:03:06,290 --> 00:03:10,911
people, is like sitting in sunshine, calm and sweet,

41
00:03:10,911 --> 00:03:14,690
serene inward feelings bud and bloom under the ray.

42
00:03:15,550 --> 00:03:20,150
At this period of my life, my heart far often as swelled with thankfulness,

43
00:03:20,610 --> 00:03:22,150
than sank with dejection.

44
00:03:23,230 --> 00:03:29,870
And yet, reader, to tell you all in the midst of this calm, this useful existence

45
00:03:30,529 --> 00:03:34,834
after a day passed in honorable exertion amongst my scholars,

46
00:03:34,834 --> 00:03:38,669
an evening spent in drawing or reading contentedly alone.

47
00:03:39,330 --> 00:03:44,690
I used to rush into strange dreams at night, dreams many colored agitated,

48
00:03:45,230 --> 00:03:51,029
full of the ideal, the stirring, the stormy, dreams where amidst unusual

49
00:03:51,031 --> 00:03:55,730
scenes charged with adventure, with agitating risk and romantic chance,

50
00:03:56,690 --> 00:04:01,830
I still again and again met Mr. Rochester, always at some exciting crisis,

51
00:04:02,610 --> 00:04:07,470
and then the sense of being in his arms, hearing his voice, meeting his eye,

52
00:04:07,970 --> 00:04:12,809
touching his hand and cheek, loving him, being loved by him.

53
00:04:13,540 --> 00:04:16,375
The hope of passing a lifetime at his side would be

54
00:04:16,377 --> 00:04:22,449
renewed, with all its first force and fire, then I awoke.

55
00:04:23,150 --> 00:04:28,309
Then I recalled where I was and how situated, then I rose up on my curtainless

56
00:04:28,311 --> 00:04:32,889
bed, trembling and quivering, and then the still dark night

57
00:04:32,891 --> 00:04:37,629
witnessed the convulsion of despair and heard the burst of passion.

58
00:04:38,650 --> 00:04:42,629
By nine o'clock the next morning I was punctually opening the school,

59
00:04:43,150 --> 00:04:47,230
tranquil, settled, prepared for the steady duties of the day.

60
00:04:49,330 --> 00:04:52,889
Rosamond Oliver kept her word in coming to visit me.

61
00:04:54,150 --> 00:04:58,290
Her call at the school was generally made in the course of her morning ride.

62
00:04:59,489 --> 00:05:05,010
She would canter up to the door on her pony, followed by a mounted livery servant.

63
00:05:05,790 --> 00:05:09,849
Anything more exquisite than her appearance in her purple habit,

64
00:05:10,569 --> 00:05:15,910
with her Amazon's cap of black velvet placed gracefully above the long curls

65
00:05:15,911 --> 00:05:22,029
that kissed her cheek and floated to her shoulders, can scarcely be imagined.

66
00:05:22,550 --> 00:05:27,216
And it was thus she would enter the rustic building and

67
00:05:27,218 --> 00:05:30,949
glide through the dazzled ranks of the village children.

68
00:05:32,050 --> 00:05:34,911
She generally came at the hour when Mr. Rivers

69
00:05:34,913 --> 00:05:38,230
was engaged in giving his daily catacizing lesson.

70
00:05:39,430 --> 00:05:45,410
Keenley, I fear, did the eye of the visitress pierce the young pastor's heart.

71
00:05:46,230 --> 00:05:52,010
A sort of instinct seemed to warn him of her entrance, even when he did not see it.

72
00:05:52,569 --> 00:05:57,889
And when he was looking quite away from the door, if she appeared at his cheek

73
00:05:57,891 --> 00:06:03,269
would glow, and his marble-seeming features, though they refused to relax,

74
00:06:04,169 --> 00:06:05,690
changed indescribably.

75
00:06:06,470 --> 00:06:12,209
And in their very quiescence, became expressive of a repressed fervor,

76
00:06:12,790 --> 00:06:16,290
stronger than working muscle or darting glance could indicate.

77
00:06:17,330 --> 00:06:20,410
Of course, she knew her power.

78
00:06:21,169 --> 00:06:25,470
Indeed, he did not, because he could not conceal it from her.

79
00:06:26,610 --> 00:06:30,589
In spite of his Christian stoicism, when she went up and addressed him,

80
00:06:31,169 --> 00:06:34,714
and smiled galley, encouragingly, even fondly in

81
00:06:34,716 --> 00:06:38,190
his face, his hand would tremble and his eye burn.

82
00:06:39,529 --> 00:06:45,190
He seemed to say, with his sad and resolute look, if he did not say it with

83
00:06:45,190 --> 00:06:49,029
his lips, I love you and I know you prefer me.

84
00:06:49,930 --> 00:06:52,389
It is not despair of success that keeps me dumb.

85
00:06:52,910 --> 00:06:56,230
If I offered my heart, I believe you would accept it.

86
00:06:56,870 --> 00:06:59,870
But that heart is already laid on a sacred altar.

87
00:07:00,690 --> 00:07:02,650
The fire is arranged round it.

88
00:07:03,370 --> 00:07:06,569
It will soon be no more than a sacrifice consumed.

89
00:07:07,669 --> 00:07:12,067
And then, she would pout like a disappointed child,

90
00:07:12,067 --> 00:07:15,550
a pensive cloud would soften her radiant vivacity.

91
00:07:16,129 --> 00:07:21,930
She would withdraw her hand hastily from his, and turn in transient petulence from

92
00:07:21,930 --> 00:07:25,889
his aspect, at once so heroic and so martyr-like.

93
00:07:26,510 --> 00:07:32,250
Sinjin, no doubt, would have given the world to follow, recall, retain her,

94
00:07:32,889 --> 00:07:33,989
when she thus left him.

95
00:07:34,849 --> 00:07:39,849
But he would not give one chance of heaven, nor relinquish for the elisium of

96
00:07:39,851 --> 00:07:44,250
her love, one hope of the true eternal paradise.

97
00:07:45,709 --> 00:07:51,110
Besides, he could not bind all that he had in his nature, the rover, the aspirant,

98
00:07:51,269 --> 00:07:54,849
the poet, the priest, in the limits of a single passion.

99
00:07:55,790 --> 00:08:00,540
He could not, he would not renounce his wild field of

100
00:08:00,542 --> 00:08:04,290
mission warfare for the parlors and the peace of Vale Hall.

101
00:08:05,330 --> 00:08:10,769
I learnt so much from himself, in an in-road I once, despite his reserve,

102
00:08:11,550 --> 00:08:13,650
had the daring to make on his confidence.

103
00:08:15,029 --> 00:08:18,589
Miss Oliver already honored me with frequent visits to my cottage.

104
00:08:19,569 --> 00:08:24,129
I had learnt her whole character, which was without mystery or disguise.

105
00:08:24,949 --> 00:08:30,570
She was cockatish, but not heartless, exacting but not worthlessly selfish.

106
00:08:31,410 --> 00:08:36,009
She had been indulged from her birth, but was not absolutely spoiled.

107
00:08:36,789 --> 00:08:39,070
She was hasty but good-humoured, vain.

108
00:08:39,970 --> 00:08:42,944
She could not help it, when every glance in the

109
00:08:42,945 --> 00:08:46,130
glass showed her such a flush of loveliness.

110
00:08:47,830 --> 00:08:52,429
But not affected, liberal-handed, innocent of the pride of wealth,

111
00:08:52,669 --> 00:08:56,869
ingenuous, sufficiently intelligent, gay, lively, and unthinking.

112
00:08:57,449 --> 00:09:03,790
She was very charming, in short, even to a cool observer of her own sex like me.

113
00:09:04,429 --> 00:09:07,649
But she was not profoundly interesting or thoroughly impressive.

114
00:09:08,470 --> 00:09:11,800
A very different sort of mind was hers from

115
00:09:11,801 --> 00:09:14,889
that, for instance, of the Sisters of Syngen.

116
00:09:15,449 --> 00:09:22,350
Still, I liked her almost as I like my pupil Adele, except that, for a child whom

117
00:09:22,350 --> 00:09:26,949
we have watched over and taught, a closer affection is engendered,

118
00:09:27,250 --> 00:09:31,009
than we can give an equally attractive adult acquaintance.

119
00:09:31,610 --> 00:09:34,990
She had taken an amiable caprice to me.

120
00:09:35,729 --> 00:09:38,949
She said I was like Mr. Rivers, only certainly.

121
00:09:39,669 --> 00:09:40,669
She allowed.

122
00:09:41,509 --> 00:09:44,486
Not one tenth so handsome, though I was a nice

123
00:09:44,486 --> 00:09:47,050
neat little soul enough, but he was an angel.

124
00:09:47,470 --> 00:09:52,369
I was however good, clever, composed, and firm like him.

125
00:09:53,110 --> 00:09:57,449
I was a lucous natural eye, she affirmed as a village school mistress.

126
00:09:58,550 --> 00:10:05,089
She was sure my previous history, if known, would make a delightful romance

127
00:10:05,990 --> 00:10:12,089
one evening, while with her usual childlike activity, and thoughtless yet

128
00:10:12,091 --> 00:10:15,418
not offensive inquisitiveness, she was rummaging the

129
00:10:15,419 --> 00:10:18,089
cupboard and the table drawer of my little kitchen.

130
00:10:18,750 --> 00:10:25,350
She discovered first two French books, a volume of shiller, a German grammar and

131
00:10:25,350 --> 00:10:31,710
dictionary, and then my drawing materials and some sketches, including a pencilhead

132
00:10:31,710 --> 00:10:36,630
of a pretty little cherubly girl, one of my scholars and sundry views from

133
00:10:36,630 --> 00:10:40,949
nature, taken in the veil of Morton and on the surrounding moors.

134
00:10:41,550 --> 00:10:47,389
She was first transfixed with surprise and then electrified with delight.

135
00:10:48,970 --> 00:10:50,470
Had I done these pictures?

136
00:10:51,309 --> 00:10:52,529
Did I know French in German?

137
00:10:53,570 --> 00:10:56,149
What a love, what a miracle I was.

138
00:10:56,990 --> 00:10:59,470
I drew better than her master in the first school in S.

139
00:11:00,029 --> 00:11:02,850
Would I sketch a portrait of her to show to Papa?

140
00:11:04,029 --> 00:11:10,210
With pleasure I replied, and I felt a thrill of artist delight at the idea of

141
00:11:10,210 --> 00:11:13,149
copying from so perfect and radiant a model.

142
00:11:14,250 --> 00:11:20,350
She had then, on a dark blue silk dress, her arms and her neck were bare,

143
00:11:21,229 --> 00:11:25,232
her only ornament was her chestnut dresses which waved over

144
00:11:25,232 --> 00:11:29,089
her shoulders with all the wild grace of natural curls.

145
00:11:30,190 --> 00:11:34,389
I took a sheet of fine cardboard and drew a careful outline.

146
00:11:35,330 --> 00:11:41,229
I promised myself the pleasure of coloring it, and as it was getting late then,

147
00:11:41,929 --> 00:11:44,449
I told her she must come and sit another day.

148
00:11:46,169 --> 00:11:49,898
She made such a report of me to her father, that

149
00:11:49,899 --> 00:11:53,250
Mr. Oliver himself accompanied her next evening.

150
00:11:53,850 --> 00:11:59,949
A tall, massive featured, middle-aged and gray-headed man, at whose side his lovely

151
00:11:59,951 --> 00:12:03,169
daughter looked like a bright flower near a horrid turret.

152
00:12:04,089 --> 00:12:11,430
He appeared a taciturn, and perhaps a proud personage, but he was very kind to me.

153
00:12:11,529 --> 00:12:14,350
The sketch of Rosamond's portrait pleased him highly.

154
00:12:15,050 --> 00:12:17,570
He said I must make a finished picture of it.

155
00:12:18,220 --> 00:12:23,110
He insisted, too, on my coming the next day to spend the evening at Vale Hall.

156
00:12:24,250 --> 00:12:25,309
I went.

157
00:12:26,429 --> 00:12:30,270
I found it a large handsome residence, showing

158
00:12:30,271 --> 00:12:33,730
abundant evidences of wealth in the proprietor.

159
00:12:34,889 --> 00:12:39,029
Rosamond was full of glee and pleasure all the time I stayed.

160
00:12:39,869 --> 00:12:44,070
Her father was affable, and when he entered into conversation with me after

161
00:12:44,070 --> 00:12:49,270
tea, he expressed in strong terms his approbation of what I had done in Morton

162
00:12:49,270 --> 00:12:55,690
School, and said he only feared, from what he saw and heard, I was too good

163
00:12:55,691 --> 00:12:59,669
for the place, and would soon quit it for one more suitable.

164
00:13:01,690 --> 00:13:03,710
Indeed, cried Rosamond.

165
00:13:04,509 --> 00:13:07,669
She is clever enough to be a governess in a high-family papar.

166
00:13:08,690 --> 00:13:13,929
I thought I would far rather be where I am than in any high-family in the land.

167
00:13:15,410 --> 00:13:21,509
Mr. Oliver spoke of Mr. Rivers, of the Rivers family, with great respect.

168
00:13:22,429 --> 00:13:28,190
He said it was a very old name in that neighborhood, that the ancestors of the

169
00:13:28,191 --> 00:13:35,149
house were wealthy, that all Morton had once belonged to them, that even now he

170
00:13:35,150 --> 00:13:38,619
considered the representative of that house might,

171
00:13:38,619 --> 00:13:41,650
if he liked, make an alliance with the best.

172
00:13:42,690 --> 00:13:47,187
He accounted it a pity that so fine and talented a young man

173
00:13:47,187 --> 00:13:50,610
should have formed the design of going out as a missionary.

174
00:13:51,449 --> 00:13:54,130
It was quite throwing a valuable life away.

175
00:13:55,229 --> 00:13:58,316
It appeared then that her father would throw no

176
00:13:58,316 --> 00:14:01,391
obstacle in the way of Rosamond's union with Syngen.

177
00:14:02,550 --> 00:14:06,949
Mr. Oliver evidently regarded the young clergyman's good-birth, old name,

178
00:14:06,951 --> 00:14:12,330
and sacred profession as sufficient compensation for the want of fortune.

179
00:14:12,949 --> 00:14:15,710
It was the 5th of November and a holiday.

180
00:14:16,550 --> 00:14:20,953
My little servant, after helping me to clean my house, was

181
00:14:20,955 --> 00:14:24,330
gone, well satisfied with the fee of a penny for her aid.

182
00:14:25,710 --> 00:14:28,842
All about me was spotless and bright, scoured

183
00:14:28,843 --> 00:14:31,910
floor, polished great and well -rubbed chairs.

184
00:14:32,990 --> 00:14:38,850
I had also made myself neat and had now the afternoon before me to spend as I would.

185
00:14:39,089 --> 00:14:43,270
The translation of a few pages of German occupied an hour.

186
00:14:44,190 --> 00:14:50,850
Then I got my palette and pencils and fell to the more soothing because easier

187
00:14:50,850 --> 00:14:54,729
occupation of completing Rosamond Oliver's miniature.

188
00:14:55,869 --> 00:14:57,369
The head was finished already.

189
00:14:58,309 --> 00:15:02,369
There was but the background to tint and the drapery to shade off.

190
00:15:03,149 --> 00:15:06,690
A touch of car-mind too to add to the ripe lips.

191
00:15:07,529 --> 00:15:10,169
A soft curl here and there to the tresses.

192
00:15:11,050 --> 00:15:14,509
A deeper tinge to the shadow of the lash under the azured eyelid.

193
00:15:15,289 --> 00:15:21,250
I was absorbed in the execution of these nice details when, after one rapid tap,

194
00:15:21,949 --> 00:15:25,149
my door unclosed, admitting Singen rivers.

195
00:15:26,210 --> 00:15:30,070
I am come to see how you are spending your holiday, he said.

196
00:15:31,029 --> 00:15:34,289
Not, I hope, in thought, know that as well.

197
00:15:35,050 --> 00:15:37,610
While you draw, you will not feel lonely.

198
00:15:38,509 --> 00:15:43,691
You see, I mistrust you still, though you have borne up wonderfully so far.

199
00:15:43,830 --> 00:15:46,190
I have brought you a book for evening solace.

200
00:15:46,690 --> 00:15:50,610
And he laid on the table a new publication, a poem.

201
00:15:51,729 --> 00:15:56,750
One of those genuine productions, so often vouchsafed to the fortunate

202
00:15:56,751 --> 00:16:01,729
public of those days, the golden age of modern literature, alas.

203
00:16:02,570 --> 00:16:06,389
The readers of our era are less favored, but courage.

204
00:16:07,470 --> 00:16:10,309
I will not pause either to accuse or repine.

205
00:16:10,809 --> 00:16:15,252
I know poetry is not dead, nor genius lost, nor has

206
00:16:15,254 --> 00:16:19,130
maman gained power over either, to bind or slay.

207
00:16:19,710 --> 00:16:21,468
They will both assert their existence, their

208
00:16:21,470 --> 00:16:24,171
presence, their liberty and strength again one day.

209
00:16:25,270 --> 00:16:27,550
Powerful angels, safe in heaven.

210
00:16:28,929 --> 00:16:34,730
They smile when sordid souls triumph, and feeble ones weep over their destruction.

211
00:16:35,610 --> 00:16:36,610
Poetry destroyed?

212
00:16:37,070 --> 00:16:38,070
Genius banished?

213
00:16:38,110 --> 00:16:39,110
No.

214
00:16:39,410 --> 00:16:40,410
Mediocrity, no.

215
00:16:41,210 --> 00:16:43,750
Do not let envy prompt you to the thought.

216
00:16:44,589 --> 00:16:45,589
No.

217
00:16:45,869 --> 00:16:48,929
They not only live, but reign and redeem.

218
00:16:49,850 --> 00:16:54,009
And without their divine influence spread everywhere, you would be in hell,

219
00:16:54,410 --> 00:16:55,910
the hell of your own meanness.

220
00:16:56,750 --> 00:17:02,050
While I was eagerly glancing at the bright pages of maman, for maman it was.

221
00:17:02,910 --> 00:17:05,389
Syngin stooped to examine my drawing.

222
00:17:06,210 --> 00:17:08,990
His tall figure sprang erect again with a start.

223
00:17:09,589 --> 00:17:10,850
He said nothing.

224
00:17:11,610 --> 00:17:12,610
I looked up at him.

225
00:17:13,289 --> 00:17:14,410
He shunned my eye.

226
00:17:15,169 --> 00:17:18,830
I knew his thoughts well, and could read his heart plainly.

227
00:17:19,449 --> 00:17:22,110
At the moment I felt calmer and cooler than he.

228
00:17:22,990 --> 00:17:26,437
I had then temporarily the advantage of him, and

229
00:17:26,437 --> 00:17:29,730
I conceived an inclination to do him some good.

230
00:17:29,970 --> 00:17:30,970
If I could.

231
00:17:32,050 --> 00:17:37,470
With all his firmness and self-control thought I, he tasks himself too far,

232
00:17:38,229 --> 00:17:43,970
locks every feeling and pang within, expresses, confesses, imparts nothing.

233
00:17:44,710 --> 00:17:48,449
I am sure it would benefit him to talk a little about this sweet rosamond,

234
00:17:48,889 --> 00:17:50,570
whom he thinks he ought not to marry.

235
00:17:51,229 --> 00:17:52,289
I will make him talk.

236
00:17:53,449 --> 00:17:54,470
I said first.

237
00:17:55,449 --> 00:17:56,729
Take a chair, Mr. Rivers.

238
00:17:57,750 --> 00:17:59,410
But he answered, as he always did.

239
00:17:59,970 --> 00:18:00,970
That he could not stay.

240
00:18:02,229 --> 00:18:04,750
Very well, I responded mentally.

241
00:18:05,130 --> 00:18:06,130
Stand if you like.

242
00:18:06,429 --> 00:18:08,029
But you shall not go just yet.

243
00:18:08,589 --> 00:18:09,589
I am determined.

244
00:18:10,270 --> 00:18:13,410
Solitude is at least as bad for you as it is for me.

245
00:18:14,550 --> 00:18:19,570
I'll try if I cannot discover the secret spring of your confidence and find an

246
00:18:19,570 --> 00:18:22,578
aperture in that marble breast through which

247
00:18:22,580 --> 00:18:26,130
I can shed one drop of the balm of sympathy.

248
00:18:27,149 --> 00:18:28,710
Is this portrait like?

249
00:18:29,210 --> 00:18:30,449
I asked bluntly.

250
00:18:31,089 --> 00:18:32,089
Like?

251
00:18:32,210 --> 00:18:33,210
Like whom?

252
00:18:33,389 --> 00:18:34,869
I did not observe it closely.

253
00:18:35,809 --> 00:18:37,490
You did, Mr. Rivers.

254
00:18:38,910 --> 00:18:42,770
He almost started at my sudden and strange abruptness.

255
00:18:43,369 --> 00:18:44,949
He looked at me astonished.

256
00:18:46,470 --> 00:18:48,389
Oh, that is nothing yet.

257
00:18:49,229 --> 00:18:50,229
I muttered within.

258
00:18:51,330 --> 00:18:54,270
I don't mean to be baffled by a little stiffness on your part.

259
00:18:54,929 --> 00:18:57,149
I'm prepared to go to considerable lengths.

260
00:18:58,449 --> 00:18:59,449
I continued.

261
00:18:59,850 --> 00:19:02,029
You observed it closely and distinctly.

262
00:19:02,550 --> 00:19:04,589
But I have no objection to your looking at it again.

263
00:19:05,029 --> 00:19:07,250
And I rose and placed it in his hand.

264
00:19:08,210 --> 00:19:10,990
A well-executed picture, he said.

265
00:19:11,669 --> 00:19:16,229
Very soft, clear coloring, very graceful and correct drawing.

266
00:19:17,309 --> 00:19:18,630
Yes, yes, I know all that.

267
00:19:19,330 --> 00:19:20,470
But what of the resemblance?

268
00:19:20,649 --> 00:19:21,649
Who is it like?

269
00:19:22,449 --> 00:19:24,690
Mastering some hesitation, he answered.

270
00:19:25,330 --> 00:19:26,910
Miss Oliver, I presume.

271
00:19:27,990 --> 00:19:28,990
Of course.

272
00:19:29,750 --> 00:19:33,449
And now, sir, to reward you for the accurate guess.

273
00:19:34,550 --> 00:19:39,710
I will promise to paint you a careful and faithful duplicate of this very picture

274
00:19:39,710 --> 00:19:44,110
provided you admit that the gift would be acceptable to you.

275
00:19:44,970 --> 00:19:49,289
I don't wish to throw away my time and trouble on an offering.

276
00:19:49,949 --> 00:19:51,350
You would deem worthless.

277
00:19:52,449 --> 00:19:54,710
He continued to gaze at the picture.

278
00:19:55,589 --> 00:20:00,770
The longer he looked, the firmer he held it, the more he seemed to cover it.

279
00:20:01,270 --> 00:20:03,130
It is like, he murmured.

280
00:20:03,830 --> 00:20:05,389
The eye is well-managed.

281
00:20:05,830 --> 00:20:07,910
The color, light expression, are perfect.

282
00:20:08,470 --> 00:20:09,470
It smiles.

283
00:20:10,830 --> 00:20:14,669
Would it comfort, or would it wound you to have a similar painting?

284
00:20:15,630 --> 00:20:22,610
Tell me that, when you are at Madagascar, or at the Cape, or in India, would it be a

285
00:20:22,611 --> 00:20:25,550
consolation to have that memento in your possession?

286
00:20:26,690 --> 00:20:32,171
Or would the sight of it bring recollections calculated to innovate and distress?

287
00:20:32,990 --> 00:20:34,809
He now furtively raised his eyes.

288
00:20:35,690 --> 00:20:36,690
He glanced at me.

289
00:20:37,229 --> 00:20:38,889
Irresolute, disturbed.

290
00:20:39,789 --> 00:20:41,429
He again surveyed the picture.

291
00:20:42,710 --> 00:20:46,194
That I should like to have it is certain, whether

292
00:20:46,195 --> 00:20:49,370
it would be judicious or wise is another question.

293
00:20:51,289 --> 00:20:55,726
Since I had ascertained that Rosamond really preferred him,

294
00:20:55,728 --> 00:20:58,729
and that her father was not likely to oppose the match.

295
00:20:59,589 --> 00:21:03,300
I, less exalted in my views than Sinjin, had been

296
00:21:03,301 --> 00:21:07,509
strongly disposed in my own heart to advocate their union.

297
00:21:09,029 --> 00:21:14,470
It seemed to me that, should he become the possessor of Mr. Oliver's large fortune,

298
00:21:15,350 --> 00:21:20,429
he might do as much good with it as if he went and laid his genius out to with her

299
00:21:20,929 --> 00:21:24,289
and his strength to waste under a tropical sun.

300
00:21:25,550 --> 00:21:31,649
With this persuasion I now answered, as far as I can see, it would be wiser and

301
00:21:31,650 --> 00:21:36,410
more judicious if you were to take to yourself the original at once.

302
00:21:37,130 --> 00:21:39,470
By this time, he had sat down.

303
00:21:40,350 --> 00:21:43,706
He had laid the picture on the table before him, and with

304
00:21:43,706 --> 00:21:48,210
his brow supported on both hands hung fondly over it.

305
00:21:49,029 --> 00:21:54,110
I discerned he was now neither angry nor shocked at my audacity.

306
00:21:55,169 --> 00:21:57,843
I saw even that to be thus frankly addressed

307
00:21:57,845 --> 00:22:00,471
on a subject he had deemed unapproachable.

308
00:22:01,169 --> 00:22:07,671
To hear it thus freely handled was beginning to be felt by him as a new pleasure.

309
00:22:08,009 --> 00:22:10,050
An unhoved for relief.

310
00:22:11,210 --> 00:22:14,658
Reserved people often really need the frank discussion

311
00:22:14,660 --> 00:22:18,289
of their sentiments and griefs more than the expansive.

312
00:22:19,309 --> 00:22:22,309
The sternest seeming stoic is human after all.

313
00:22:23,229 --> 00:22:29,229
And to burst with boldness and goodwill into the silent sea of their souls is

314
00:22:29,230 --> 00:22:32,729
often to confer on them the first of occasions.

315
00:22:33,949 --> 00:22:38,350
She likes you, I am sure, said I, as I stood behind his chair.

316
00:22:39,369 --> 00:22:41,009
And her father respects you.

317
00:22:42,029 --> 00:22:46,990
Moreover, she is a sweet girl, rather thoughtless, but you would have

318
00:22:46,990 --> 00:22:49,190
sufficient thought for both yourself and her.

319
00:22:49,830 --> 00:22:51,089
You ought to marry her.

320
00:22:52,789 --> 00:22:53,789
Does she like me?

321
00:22:54,589 --> 00:22:58,529
He asked, certainly, better than she likes anyone else.

322
00:22:59,509 --> 00:23:01,490
She talks of you continually.

323
00:23:02,270 --> 00:23:06,149
There is no subject she enjoys so much or touches upon so often.

324
00:23:07,669 --> 00:23:14,691
It is very pleasant to hear this, he said, very go on for another quarter of an hour.

325
00:23:15,429 --> 00:23:20,611
And he actually took out his watch and laid it upon the table to measure the time.

326
00:23:21,529 --> 00:23:24,350
But where is the use of going on?

327
00:23:25,229 --> 00:23:30,270
I asked, when you are probably preparing some iron blow of contradiction,

328
00:23:31,029 --> 00:23:33,869
or forging a fresh chain to fetter your heart.

329
00:23:35,009 --> 00:23:37,270
Don't imagine such hard things.

330
00:23:38,149 --> 00:23:40,350
Fancy me yielding and melting as I am doing.

331
00:23:40,949 --> 00:23:44,247
Human love, rising like a freshly opened fountain

332
00:23:44,248 --> 00:23:47,570
in my mind, and overflowing with sweet inundation.

333
00:23:48,130 --> 00:23:54,789
All the field I have so carefully and with such labour prepared, so assiduously sewn

334
00:23:54,790 --> 00:23:59,149
with the seeds of good intentions, of self-denying plans.

335
00:23:59,910 --> 00:24:03,490
And now it is deluged with a nectoris flood.

336
00:24:04,210 --> 00:24:08,570
The young germs swamped, delicious poison cancoring them.

337
00:24:09,190 --> 00:24:13,250
Now I see myself stretched on an ottoman in the drawing-room at Vale Hall.

338
00:24:14,089 --> 00:24:16,389
At my bride, Rosamond Oliver's feet.

339
00:24:17,210 --> 00:24:19,630
She is talking to me with her sweet voice.

340
00:24:20,570 --> 00:24:25,270
Gazing down on me with those eyes, your skillful hand has copied so well.

341
00:24:26,029 --> 00:24:28,009
Smiling at me with these coral lips.

342
00:24:28,630 --> 00:24:29,630
She is mine.

343
00:24:30,070 --> 00:24:31,070
I am hers.

344
00:24:31,509 --> 00:24:33,789
This present life and passing world suffice to me.

345
00:24:34,570 --> 00:24:35,830
Hush, say nothing.

346
00:24:36,570 --> 00:24:37,949
My heart is full of delight.

347
00:24:38,570 --> 00:24:40,149
My senses are entranced.

348
00:24:40,649 --> 00:24:42,369
Let the time I marked passing peace.

349
00:24:43,509 --> 00:24:44,509
I humid him.

350
00:24:44,889 --> 00:24:45,889
The watch ticked on.

351
00:24:45,970 --> 00:24:47,389
He breathed fast and low.

352
00:24:47,889 --> 00:24:48,889
I stood silent.

353
00:24:50,550 --> 00:24:52,690
Amidst this hush, the quartet sped.

354
00:24:53,149 --> 00:24:58,089
He replaced the watch, laid the picture down, rose, and stood on the hearth.

355
00:24:59,449 --> 00:25:01,369
Now said he.

356
00:25:02,389 --> 00:25:05,289
That little space was given to delirium and delusion.

357
00:25:06,250 --> 00:25:09,854
I rested my temples on the breast of temptation and

358
00:25:09,855 --> 00:25:13,009
put my neck voluntarily under her yoke of flowers.

359
00:25:13,910 --> 00:25:15,009
I tasted her cup.

360
00:25:15,830 --> 00:25:16,830
The pillow was burning.

361
00:25:17,529 --> 00:25:19,029
There is an ass in the garland.

362
00:25:19,690 --> 00:25:20,970
The wine has a bitter taste.

363
00:25:21,649 --> 00:25:22,729
Her promises are hollow.

364
00:25:22,949 --> 00:25:23,949
Her offers false.

365
00:25:24,029 --> 00:25:25,449
I see and know all this.

366
00:25:26,949 --> 00:25:28,970
I gazed at him in wonder.

367
00:25:29,889 --> 00:25:35,729
It is strange, pursued he, that while I love Rosamond Oliver so wildly,

368
00:25:36,410 --> 00:25:41,389
with all the intensity indeed of a first passion, the object of which is

369
00:25:41,391 --> 00:25:45,289
exquisitely beautiful, graceful, fascinating.

370
00:25:46,229 --> 00:25:50,126
I experience at the same time a calm, unwrapped

371
00:25:50,126 --> 00:25:53,910
consciousness that she would not make me a good wife.

372
00:25:54,990 --> 00:25:56,949
That she is not the partner suited to me.

373
00:25:57,869 --> 00:26:03,190
That I should discover this within a year after marriage, and that a twelve-months

374
00:26:03,191 --> 00:26:06,089
rapture would succeed a lifetime of regret.

375
00:26:07,229 --> 00:26:08,470
This I know.

376
00:26:10,009 --> 00:26:12,789
Strange indeed, I could not help ejaculating.

377
00:26:14,130 --> 00:26:19,289
While something in me, he went on, is acutely sensible to her charms.

378
00:26:19,929 --> 00:26:23,309
Something else is as deeply impressed with her defects.

379
00:26:24,130 --> 00:26:29,050
They are such that she could sympathize in nothing I aspire to.

380
00:26:29,690 --> 00:26:32,210
Cooperate in nothing I undertook.

381
00:26:33,110 --> 00:26:36,470
Rosamond a sufferer, a labourer, a female apostle.

382
00:26:37,410 --> 00:26:38,990
Rosamond a missionary's wife?

383
00:26:39,610 --> 00:26:40,610
No.

384
00:26:41,089 --> 00:26:42,970
But you need not be a missionary.

385
00:26:43,850 --> 00:26:45,490
You might relinquish that scheme.

386
00:26:46,809 --> 00:26:47,809
Relinquish.

387
00:26:48,009 --> 00:26:48,169
What?

388
00:26:48,649 --> 00:26:49,649
My vocation?

389
00:26:49,910 --> 00:26:50,910
My great work?

390
00:26:51,309 --> 00:26:53,929
My foundation laid on earth for a mansion in heaven?

391
00:26:54,710 --> 00:26:59,789
My hopes have been numbered in the band, who have merged all ambitions in the

392
00:26:59,790 --> 00:27:06,029
glorious one of bettering their race, of carrying knowledge into the realms of

393
00:27:06,031 --> 00:27:10,331
ignorance, of substituting peace for war,

394
00:27:10,332 --> 00:27:14,551
freedom for bondage, religion for superstition.

395
00:27:14,750 --> 00:27:18,149
The hope of heaven for the fear of hell must I relinquish that.

396
00:27:19,330 --> 00:27:21,210
It is dearer than the blood in my veins.

397
00:27:22,089 --> 00:27:25,270
It is what I have to look forward to and to live for.

398
00:27:26,550 --> 00:27:31,070
After a considerable pause, I said, and Miss Oliver?

399
00:27:31,889 --> 00:27:34,550
Are her disappointment and sorrow of no interest to you?

400
00:27:36,250 --> 00:27:40,149
Miss Oliver is ever surrounded by shooters and flatters.

401
00:27:40,889 --> 00:27:44,929
In less than a month, my image will be a face from her heart.

402
00:27:45,550 --> 00:27:49,373
She will forget me, and will marry, probably, someone

403
00:27:49,373 --> 00:27:52,490
who will make her far happier than I should do.

404
00:27:53,830 --> 00:27:57,169
You speak cool enough, but you suffer in the conflict.

405
00:28:02,529 --> 00:28:06,350
You are with anxiety about my prospects, yet unsettled.

406
00:28:07,130 --> 00:28:10,470
My departure continually procrastinated.

407
00:28:11,669 --> 00:28:17,490
Only this morning, I received intelligence that the successor, whose arrival I have

408
00:28:17,490 --> 00:28:22,910
been so long expecting, cannot be ready to replace me for three months to come yet.

409
00:28:23,970 --> 00:28:26,610
And perhaps the three months may extend to six.

410
00:28:28,190 --> 00:28:32,389
You tremble and become flushed whenever Miss Oliver enters the schoolroom.

411
00:28:33,229 --> 00:28:36,690
Again, the surprised expression crossed his face.

412
00:28:37,490 --> 00:28:41,029
He had not imagined that a woman would dare to speak so to a man.

413
00:28:42,149 --> 00:28:45,789
For me, I felt at home in this sort of discourse.

414
00:28:46,690 --> 00:28:49,349
I could never rest in communication with strong

415
00:28:49,350 --> 00:28:52,350
discreet and refined minds whether male or female.

416
00:28:52,850 --> 00:28:57,509
Till I had passed the outworks of conventional reserve and crossed the

417
00:28:57,510 --> 00:29:03,009
threshold of confidence and won a place by their heart's very hearth stone.

418
00:29:04,869 --> 00:29:08,770
You are original, said he, and not timid.

419
00:29:09,690 --> 00:29:14,110
There is something brave in your spirit, as well as penetrating in your eye.

420
00:29:15,070 --> 00:29:19,449
But allow me to assure you that you partially misinterpret my emotions.

421
00:29:20,350 --> 00:29:23,210
You think them more profound and potent than they are.

422
00:29:23,949 --> 00:29:27,990
You give me a larger allowance of sympathy than I have just claimed to.

423
00:29:29,389 --> 00:29:35,250
When I colour and when I shake before Miss Oliver, I do not pity myself.

424
00:29:36,050 --> 00:29:37,369
I scorn the weakness.

425
00:29:38,270 --> 00:29:41,490
I know it is ignoble, a mere fever of the flesh.

426
00:29:42,130 --> 00:29:46,830
Not, I declare, the convulsion of the soul that is just as fixed as a rock,

427
00:29:47,250 --> 00:29:49,550
firm set in the depths of a restless sea.

428
00:29:50,270 --> 00:29:52,729
Know me to be what I am, a cold hard man.

429
00:29:53,729 --> 00:29:55,509
I smiled incredulously.

430
00:29:56,550 --> 00:29:59,388
You have taken my confidence by storm, he

431
00:29:59,389 --> 00:30:03,251
continued, and now it is much at your service.

432
00:30:03,729 --> 00:30:09,449
I am simply, in my original state, stripped of that blood bleached robe with

433
00:30:09,451 --> 00:30:13,929
which Christianity covers human deformity, a cold hard ambitious man.

434
00:30:14,770 --> 00:30:20,149
Natural affection only of all the sentiments has permanent power over me.

435
00:30:21,169 --> 00:30:24,470
Reason and not feeling is my guide.

436
00:30:25,369 --> 00:30:26,990
My ambition is unlimited.

437
00:30:28,029 --> 00:30:32,410
My desire to rise higher, to do more than others insatiable.

438
00:30:33,190 --> 00:30:39,429
I honour endurance, perseverance, industry, talent, because these are the

439
00:30:39,430 --> 00:30:44,789
means by which men achieve great ends and mount to lofty eminence.

440
00:30:45,410 --> 00:30:50,610
I watch your career with interest, because I consider you a specimen of a

441
00:30:50,611 --> 00:30:57,029
diligent, orderly, energetic woman, not because I deeply compassionate what

442
00:30:57,031 --> 00:30:59,910
you have gone through or what you still suffer.

443
00:31:01,589 --> 00:31:06,389
You would describe yourself as a mere pagan philosopher, I said.

444
00:31:08,429 --> 00:31:09,149
No.

445
00:31:09,150 --> 00:31:12,830
There is this difference between me and deistic philosophers.

446
00:31:13,949 --> 00:31:16,770
I believe, and I believe the gospel.

447
00:31:17,710 --> 00:31:18,949
You missed your epithet.

448
00:31:19,490 --> 00:31:24,910
I am not a pagan, but a Christian philosopher, a follower of the sect of Jesus.

449
00:31:24,949 --> 00:31:30,190
As his disciple I adopt his pure, his merciful, his benignant doctrines,

450
00:31:30,750 --> 00:31:31,750
I advocate them.

451
00:31:32,119 --> 00:31:33,929
I am sworn to spread them.

452
00:31:35,610 --> 00:31:40,190
One in youth to religion, she has cultivated my original qualities thus.

453
00:31:41,350 --> 00:31:46,429
From the minute germ, natural affection, she has developed the overshadowing tree,

454
00:31:46,970 --> 00:31:47,970
Philanthropy.

455
00:31:48,449 --> 00:31:52,407
From the wild stringy root of human uprightness,

456
00:31:52,408 --> 00:31:55,850
she has reared a due sense of the divine justice.

457
00:31:56,729 --> 00:32:02,830
Of the ambition to win power and renown for my wretched self, she has formed the

458
00:32:02,831 --> 00:32:06,115
ambition to spread my master's kingdom, to

459
00:32:06,115 --> 00:32:10,130
achieve victories for the standard of the cross.

460
00:32:10,869 --> 00:32:14,267
So much has religion done for me, turning the original

461
00:32:14,267 --> 00:32:18,830
materials to the best account, pruning and training nature.

462
00:32:20,029 --> 00:32:24,216
But she could not eradicate nature, nor will it be

463
00:32:24,217 --> 00:32:27,710
eradicated, till this mortal shall put on immortality.

464
00:32:28,710 --> 00:32:33,190
Having said this, he took his hat, which lay on the table beside my pallet.

465
00:32:33,910 --> 00:32:35,410
Once more he looked at the portrait.

466
00:32:36,750 --> 00:32:38,850
She is lovely, he murmured.

467
00:32:39,570 --> 00:32:42,529
She is well named the rose of the world indeed.

468
00:32:43,750 --> 00:32:46,729
And may I not paint one like it for you?

469
00:32:47,750 --> 00:32:48,990
Quibono, no.

470
00:32:49,729 --> 00:32:54,690
He drew over the picture, the sheet of thin paper on which I was accustomed to

471
00:32:54,691 --> 00:32:58,830
rest my hand in painting, to prevent the cardboard from being solid.

472
00:33:00,190 --> 00:33:05,509
What he suddenly saw on this blank paper, it was impossible for me to tell.

473
00:33:05,510 --> 00:33:08,470
But something had caught his eye.

474
00:33:09,369 --> 00:33:10,490
He took it up with a snatch.

475
00:33:11,369 --> 00:33:14,880
He looked at the edge, then shot a glance at me,

476
00:33:14,880 --> 00:33:18,190
inexpressibly peculiar and quite incomprehensible.

477
00:33:19,070 --> 00:33:23,990
A glance that seemed to take and make note of every point in my shape, face and

478
00:33:23,990 --> 00:33:28,429
dress, for it traversed all, quick, keen as lightning.

479
00:33:29,250 --> 00:33:33,350
His lips parted as if to speak, but he checked the coming sentence,

480
00:33:33,570 --> 00:33:34,570
whatever it was.

481
00:33:35,509 --> 00:33:37,529
What is the matter, I asked?

482
00:33:38,270 --> 00:33:40,410
Nothing in the world was the reply.

483
00:33:41,289 --> 00:33:47,150
And replacing the paper, I saw him dexterously tear and narrow slip from the margin.

484
00:33:47,309 --> 00:33:52,830
It disappeared in his glove, and with one hasty nod and good afternoon, he vanished.

485
00:33:53,910 --> 00:33:58,229
Well, I exclaimed, using an expression of the district, that caps the globe,

486
00:33:58,410 --> 00:33:59,410
however.

487
00:34:00,009 --> 00:34:06,949
I, in my turn, scrutinized the paper, but saw nothing on it save a few dingy

488
00:34:06,951 --> 00:34:10,610
stains of paint, where I had tried the tint in my pencil.

489
00:34:12,070 --> 00:34:16,150
I pondered the mystery a minute or two, but finding it

490
00:34:16,152 --> 00:34:19,910
insolvable and being certain it could not be of much moment.

491
00:34:20,729 --> 00:34:23,570
I dismissed and soon forgot it.
